==Old English==

===Etymology===
Common Germanic, from Indo-European ''*leb-, *lob-''.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''slepa'', Old High German ''[[slafan|slāfan]]'' (German ''[[schlafen]]''), Old Saxon ''slāpan'' (Dutch ''[[slapen]]''), Gothic [[𐍃𐌻𐌴𐍀𐌰𐌽]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/'slæ:p.ɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=VII|head=slǣpan}} ({{Latinx|'''slǣpþ'''}} ‘he sleeps’; {{Latinx|'''slēp'''}} ‘he slept’; {{Latinx|'''slēpon'''}} ‘they slept’; {{Latinx|'''ġeslǣpen'''}} past participle)

